-- and the refinement, in the one direction it holds: atoms the configurations keep apart may be
-- identified by the bond graph, never the other way. So a signal count read off the graph is an upper
-- bound on the equivalences that hold, and the three verdicts are now properties of one object: the graph
-- identifies a pair (at-h-one-orbit), the configuration separates it (cyc-swap-differs), and a medium
-- admitting reflections identifies it again (cyc-mirror-swap-same).
st-orbit-refines : (C : Stereo) → (x : mol-atoms (st-mol C)) → (y : mol-atoms (st-mol C)) → StOrbit C x y → Orbit (st-mol C) x y
st-orbit-refines C x y o = (fst (fst o) , snd o)
